# Corpus fixture images.
#
# The manifests beside them are committed: they are small, reviewable text, and
# a change to one is a visible change in what the library is expected to find.
# The images they describe are not, because they are megabytes of binary each.
#
# Rebuild them from the corpus with:
#
#	sudo tools/corpus/mkcorpus.sh
#	sudo tools/corpus/mkoracle.sh
#	sudo tools/corpus/mkfixtures.sh
#
# TestCommittedCorpusFixtures skips any case whose image is absent, so the
# suite passes without them and checks them wherever they have been built.
testdata/corpus/*/image.img.gz

# Filesystem images of any kind. This package's whole subject matter is disk
# images, and they are large by nature; none of them belong in the repository.
*.img
*.img.gz
*.metadump
*.dd

# Compiled binaries.
*.exe
*.test

# Built example programs. A whitelist rather than a pattern for
# extensionless binaries, which would also match the sources next to them.
/examples/*/*
!/examples/*/*.go
!/examples/*/*.md

# Go's fuzz cache. Failing inputs under testdata/fuzz are deliberately kept:
# they are a few bytes each and are what stops a crash from coming back.
/fuzz-cache/
